Task: Parked-car kinds + authored map instances (FR1, FR9) — Phase 1, task 1

Summary of changes:
- Parked-car prop kinds (parkedSedan, parkedHatchback, parkedVan, parkedSuv)
  added to the town's prop union, with a type guard so the circle-only paths
  cannot be handed a parked car by accident.
- The four Car Kit models measured into PARKED_CAR_EXTENTS (length/width) so a
  footprint can be derived before the art is mounted, plus PARKED_CAR_FIT
  (0.55), PARKED_CAR_KERB_OFFSET (0.46) and parkedCarFootprint(), which throws
  on a yaw that is not a quarter turn.
- Six instances authored in townMap.ts on the streets they park against, four
  of them on kerbs whose house wall measures >= 0.652 from the street's centre
  line, two facing the other way so a street does not read as a parade.
- createTownGrid publishes, per parked prop, the authored yaw and the
  axis-aligned half extents already swapped by it; collisionRadius becomes
  optional and is absent for parked cars; collectObstacles lists only the props
  that carry a radius. Parked-car model URLs join the registry and TOWN_MODELS.

Files created:
- src/game/town/parkedCars.test.ts (12 tests, written first and failing on a
  missing data layer before the implementation landed)

Files modified:
- src/game/town/townTypes.ts, townMap.ts, townGrid.ts
- src/game/assets/modelRegistry.ts (+ its test's group list)
- src/game/town/townLayout.ts (resolves the parked model URL and keeps the
  authored yaw when planning the mount)
- src/game/collision/collision.ts (+ its crashable-props assertion)

Why:
The placement work in the next task has to prove a lane-clearance and
wall-clearance contract, and it can only do that if the cars' geometry exists as
pure data first. Two pre-existing assertions were updated rather than worked
around: the registry test enumerates the model groups (parked cars are a new
group) and the collision test asserted that every prop becomes a circle — the
contract this task deliberately changes for parked cars.

Verification: pnpm check, pnpm typecheck, CI=true pnpm test (633 tests, 51
files) green; coverage on the touched logic — townGrid.ts 100%, townMap.ts
100%, townTypes.ts 95.45% (the untested line is the diagonal-yaw throw, whose
test belongs to the Phase 2 hitbox task).
